@page "/scoreboard"
@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model ScoreboardModel
@*
    The three bands phase 3 fills, none of them denominated in money.

    Two rules govern this page and both are visible in its shape. Long and short are two
    blocks rather than one table with a direction column, because any figure that would
    require adding a long result to a short result is not displayed at all. And every panel
    carries its own count and the condition under which it reads badly, because a number
    without a denominator is how you read a pattern into forty observations, and a
    scoreboard that can only show good news is decoration.
*@
<h1>@Model.Item.Title</h1>
<p class="lede">@Model.Item.What.</p>

@if (!Model.Scoreboard.HasPanels)
{
    <div class="empty-state">
        <p><b>Nothing to show yet.</b> @Model.Scoreboard.Absent.</p>
        <p>The panels fill as outcomes accumulate. Band 1 needs ten sessions to pass after a
           setup is flagged before that setup has anything to contribute, so an empty
           scoreboard on a lab that started this week is the correct reading rather than a
           fault.</p>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <p class="muted">As of @Model.Scoreboard.AsOf.</p>

    <section class="scoreboard-band">
        <h2>Band 0 — health</h2>
        <p class="muted">Is the record itself sound. Nothing below this line means anything if
           this band does not.</p>
        <dl class="panels">
            @foreach (PanelView panel in Model.Scoreboard.Health)
            {
                <div class="panel">
                    <dt>@panel.Title</dt>
                    <dd>
                        <span class="figure">@panel.Figure</span>
                        <span class="count">@panel.Count</span>
                        <span class="over">@panel.Over</span>
                        @if (panel.ReadsBadlyWhen is string warns)
                        {
                            <span class="warns">@warns</span>
                        }
                    </dd>
                </div>
            }
        </dl>
    </section>

    @foreach ((string side, IReadOnlyList<PanelView> panels) in
        new[] { ("Long", Model.Scoreboard.Long), ("Short", Model.Scoreboard.Short) })
    {
        <section class="scoreboard-band side">
            <h2>@side</h2>

            @if (panels.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="muted">No panels on this side yet.</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <dl class="panels">
                    @foreach (PanelView panel in panels)
                    {
                        <div class="panel @(panel.Withheld ? "withheld" : string.Empty)">
                            <dt>@panel.Title</dt>
                            <dd>
                                @if (panel.Withheld)
                                {
                                    @*
                                        Withheld rather than shown wide. A panel printing an
                                        interval built from a handful of nights invites a
                                        reading, and the count beside it is not enough to
                                        stop that.
                                    *@
                                    <span class="figure muted">withheld</span>
                                    <span class="count">@panel.Count</span>
                                    <span class="over">@panel.Over</span>

                                    @*
                                        Why, in words. Withholding is about sessions and the
                                        minimum is about evidence, they are settled by
                                        different things, and they can disagree: a fortnight
                                        of very wide nights reaches the minimum before it
                                        reaches twenty sessions.
                                    *@
                                    @if (panel.WithheldBecause is string because)
                                    {
                                        <span class="withheld-because">@because</span>
                                    }
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="figure">@panel.Figure</span>

                                    @if (panel.Interval is string interval)
                                    {
                                        <span class="interval @(panel.ClearsZero == true ? "clears" : "does-not-clear")">
                                            @interval
                                            @(panel.ClearsZero == true ? "clears zero" : "does not clear zero yet")
                                        </span>
                                    }

                                    <span class="count">@panel.Count</span>
                                    <span class="over">@panel.Over</span>
                                }

                                @*
                                    The trigger, on the panel it fires on. 3.6 used to wait
                                    three months; it now waits for the effective count to
                                    reach the minimum, and a trigger nobody can see from the
                                    first night is a date in disguise.
                                *@
                                @*
                                    Both halves of the trigger, and the one that is short is named.
                                    3.6 fires on twenty sessions AND 262 effective observations,
                                    which are settled by different things; this block compared the
                                    effective count alone and rendered the sentence of the whole
                                    condition, so a fortnight of very wide nights would have
                                    announced the trigger on a panel the bootstrap had refused to
                                    give an interval to.
                                *@
                                @if (panel.Reached is bool reached)
                                {
                                    <span class="minimum @(reached ? "reached" : "waiting")">
                                        @(reached
                                            ? "both conditions are reached: the sessions and the minimum sample"
                                            : "below the minimum sample, so this panel is not yet an answer")
                                        @if (!reached && panel.ShortOf is string shortOf)
                                        {
                                            <span class="short-of">short of @shortOf</span>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                }

                                @if (panel.ReadsBadlyWhen is string warns)
                                {
                                    <span class="warns">@warns</span>
                                }
                            </dd>
                        </div>
                    }
                </dl>
            }
        </section>
    }
}

@*
    Band 2's loss-cause panels are rendered above, in the two side blocks, because that is where
    every per-direction panel goes. The empty state that stood here until 4.11 said they arrive at
    4.10, and 4.10 built them: a placeholder outliving the thing it was standing in for reads as a
    page that has not been finished, which is the same fault as an empty state dropped too early
    read from the other side.

    Band 3 says what the page lacks structurally rather than what today happens to hold, so it
    renders whether or not any panel was built. A band that appeared only on days with data would
    be absent exactly when a reader was most likely to conclude the page had shown everything it
    has.
*@
<section class="scoreboard-band">
    <h2>Band 3 — is the loop learning</h2>
    <div class="empty-state">
        <p><b>Arrives at checkpoint 6.8.</b> Proposal outcomes by pack version, which needs the
           research loop to exist.</p>
    </div>
</section>
